;; 293.4d-fix — members written OUTSIDE the single `[...]` vector must be a HARD ERROR.
;; This is the stale `definterface` shape (field in the vector, method members as separate
;; top-level args). Arc 278 S4c (2026-07-07) made `:nature` MANDATORY, so a fixture missing it
;; now dies at the arity gate BEFORE the parser ever reaches the member-vector logic this probe
;; exists to pin — Phase 3 repair adds the mandatory `:nature`/`:features` clauses back so the
;; leftover-args-after-the-member-vector case is reachable again: `(area …) / (label …)` are
;; written as separate top-level forms AFTER the `:features [...]` member vector instead of
;; inside it, which USED to be silently dropped and after 293.4d-fix is a hard error.

(:wat::core::defsurface :t::Bad :nature :wat::core::Struct
  :features [color <- :wat::core::String]
  (area  [self] -> :wat::core::f64)
  (label [self] -> :wat::core::String))
